msgid "Contributing Local Tools to ToolUniverse"
msgstr "将本地工具贡献至 ToolUniverse"

#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/contributing/local_tools.rst:4
#: 66e803611327450c8b0507593ee3cc8a
msgid ""
"This guide covers how to contribute local Python tools to the "
"ToolUniverse repository. Local tools run within the ToolUniverse process "
"and are available to all users."
msgstr ""
"本指南介绍了如何将本地 Python 工具贡献到 ToolUniverse 仓库。本地工具在 ToolUniverse "
"进程中运行，并可供所有用户使用。"

#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/contributing/local_tools.rst:7
#: a6d557c066d9404691ebeb5846568d3f
msgid ""
"**Key Difference**: Contributing to the repository requires additional "
"steps compared to using tools locally. The most critical step is "
"modifying ``__init__.py`` in 4 specific locations."
msgstr "**关键区别**：向代码库贡献内容相比于本地使用工具需要额外的步骤。最关键的步骤是修改 ``__init__.py`` 文件中的 4 个特定位置。"

#: ../../expand_tooluniverse/contributing/local_tools.rst:10
#: 0702b79740a248e2aab24bac27a381d0
msgid ""
"**For Local Development Only**: If you just want to use a tool locally "
"without contributing to the repository, see the single-file example in "
"``examples/my_new_tool/single_file_example.py``. This approach doesn't "
"require modifying any core ToolUniverse files (``__init__.py``, "
"``default_config.py``, or ``data/`` directory). The complete working "
"examples are available in ``examples/my_new_tool/`` directory with a "
"README explaining both approaches."
msgstr ""

